<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:29Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>India: Delhi surpasses Lahore as world's most polluted city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de9711393eba14cb0d153f0a3e7426f71d11f884f609693ef93be435df99f889</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-delhi-surpasses-lahore-as-world-s-most-polluted-city/live-79946817--53d17bc3619e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-delhi-surpasses-lahore-as-world-s-most-polluted-city/live-79946817?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Delhi's Air Quality Index (AQI) was recorded to be higher than Lahore in Pakistan on Friday, which made it the most polluted city globally.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests: Do Baby Boomers really have it better than young people?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79b2093dde681620428db8e296d2a32e82769fc1813c777027ca72a9acf00259</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854--e581c42657a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Should young people in Germany be more worried about their future than Baby Boomers were in the 1980s and 1990s? Or should both generations take to the streets and protest together? DW checked the data.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal Youth Olympics in Dakar end on high note</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec4f69c90361563c88123a57d2392fe92116b2b293ce26920d33d40b4c710e00</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T04:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-youth-olympics-in-dakar-end-on-high-note/a-79944820--d8ec73fdda7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-youth-olympics-in-dakar-end-on-high-note/a-79944820?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Enthusiastic crowds attended the games in Senegal, with China taking home the most gold medals. It's the first Olympic Games since Russia's war on Ukraine where Russian athletes can compete under their own flag.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump to meet Xi, Putin for three-way huddle on nuclear arms talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54c6583d9496bfcf438333e9c89535ae2e19045a7bcae3dbbfd3b7458e647702</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T04:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-to-meet-xi-putin-for-three-way-huddle-on-nuclear-arms-talks/a-79946408--68d06493f128.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-to-meet-xi-putin-for-three-way-huddle-on-nuclear-arms-talks/a-79946408?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The White House has said President Donald Trump will urge Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin to discuss cutting nuclear arsenals in Shenzhen next week, though a senior US official expects no agreement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>SpaceX launches Starship rocket, fails to recover booster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9168d689972f1b4b1f47c5c71e15041f9e2f6fc3d107e5efc562a0f91e254701</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T02:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spacex-launches-starship-rocket-fails-to-recover-booster/a-79946091--bd09d60b45a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spacex-launches-starship-rocket-fails-to-recover-booster/a-79946091?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">SpaceX had planned to catch and later reuse both stages of its biggest rocket for the first time. But the booster exploded over the Gulf of Mexico, while the spacecraft continued into orbit.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US lifts nationwide ground stop for airports hours after halting all departures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f80f478b92f96ff96def0e8aab87922974110b17192b71ff96c65dbcae93fcb</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T01:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-lifts-nationwide-ground-stop-for-airports-hours-after-halting-all-departures/a-79945062--ab4e85db51f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-lifts-nationwide-ground-stop-for-airports-hours-after-halting-all-departures/a-79945062?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US federal aviation regulator has lifted a nationwide ground stop for all airports. Trump administration officials blame "overloaded" and "outdated" systems for the hourslong halt to departures.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tanker collides with cruise ship on Mississippi in New Orleans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e021802eab67da8aa95a80a256251d7bf2d134f1895271b042ec0b0f17e45727</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tanker-collides-with-cruise-ship-on-mississippi-in-new-orleans/a-79945080--29dd618b519d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tanker-collides-with-cruise-ship-on-mississippi-in-new-orleans/a-79945080?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A freighter collided with a cruise ship carrying around 130 people in New Orleans, causing the paddlewheel vessel to capsize. More than 30 people were hospitalized, but all passengers survived and were accounted for.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine updates: Europe to send united front to potential peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b73e3757154e4db84a78e229a346e9f90a8f292b03654a1b5b163e5615ed6677</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-europe-to-send-united-front-to-potential-peace-talks/live-79937459--c475e3dc5244.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-europe-to-send-united-front-to-potential-peace-talks/live-79937459?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany, France, the UK, Italy and Poland — as well as the EU itself — will jointly represent Europe in possible peace talks. Meanwhile, a second car bomb in two days has exploded in Moscow.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>David Walliams: UK police launch sex offense probe into comedian</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bcb2f5603aaab1c70084f0c14062c94418f99f314c034befb686d426bb35bd3</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/david-walliams-uk-police-launch-sex-offense-probe-into-comedian/a-79944161--cffd271a388c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/david-walliams-uk-police-launch-sex-offense-probe-into-comedian/a-79944161?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The "Little Britain" star and "Britain's Got Talent" judge has been accused of engaging in sexual misconduct and inappropriate behavior towards young women and girls. Walliams denies the allegations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo celebrates Mass in his former diocese of Chiclayo, Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34517acfc9ad7fb53bc926bdd387350a8cb8ee3d0c8d4fe9fb64e8693ab637d8</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T18:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-celebrates-mass-in-his-former-diocese-of-chiclayo-peru/a-79944167--e8ccd3bfe138.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-celebrates-mass-in-his-former-diocese-of-chiclayo-peru/a-79944167?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over a million people have gathered for Mass with Pope Leo XIV on Friday. The event in northern Peru, where he served as bishop before becoming head of the Catholic Church, is the centerpiece of his South American tour.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The dangers of revising Europe's security architecture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31e27889605b1b61969eba6da4f3ba0d3cf96ad05f16076750c2b686cd5234d6</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049--ae25152ee718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts warn against revising Europe's security framework because they say it would mean granting Moscow its longstanding wish of renegotiating postwar security on the continent.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders urged to 'act now' to stay AI competitive with US, China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96435822515983c5dce40b4ffb96886163dd64e304f74b93729660162d71f89f</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urged-to-act-now-to-stay-ai-competitive-with-us-china/a-79937463--41561118bdc0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urged-to-act-now-to-stay-ai-competitive-with-us-china/a-79937463?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders in Dublin were called on by an AI executive to move quickly in the tech race with the US and China. EU official Metsola, however, expressed frustration with the idea that the bloc is behind in AI development.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What's going on with the polar vortex?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5df8e9492c33e874e41b811cc466bcfc41be99e0c2b6cd86d661f217e879bafd</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105--6a28f0640609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Observations show the ring of fierce winds that rotate at the Earth's North Pole has changed direction. Scientists say it's a historic disruption and the earliest reversal on record. What could it mean for the weather?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey: Russia threatens against Canada and Germany over exclusion from tournaments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebce1a353b4ce9e5a072a7fac34f977dcd8554a47f19f344bd9cd8bf03205354</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-russia-threatens-against-canada-and-germany-over-exclusion-from-tournaments/a-79942676--747c5baa6347.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-russia-threatens-against-canada-and-germany-over-exclusion-from-tournaments/a-79942676?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fortnight after the CAS ordered ice hockey's governing body to reintegrate Russia into international play, a solution remains elusive. Now Russia has threatened to take legal action against two tournament hosts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why does El Salvador's Bukele have troops in Haiti?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b337db2188953a3e51bfb082645f3aeab20145f3b0330bba21a080a4adc7b129</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-does-el-salvador-s-bukele-have-troops-in-haiti/a-79940771--dfce4a53e7c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-does-el-salvador-s-bukele-have-troops-in-haiti/a-79940771?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Haiti's Prime Minister congratulating El Salvador's President for a gang crackdown in Haiti has shone a light on the relationship between the two countries. What's going on, and where does the US stand?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran targeted US radar system in Bahrain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4825a2b88d121f0adad662f4dbe1de67fdc1c23e88d5981787c28ea05a8859cc</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-targeted-us-radar-system-in-bahrain/a-79942640--6a6890129eef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-targeted-us-radar-system-in-bahrain/a-79942640?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran claimed it struck US radar systems in Bahrain, while the US said it had intercepted the attacks. Clashes continue in the Strait of Hormuz, as the war remains in a state of de-escalation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Beijing faces its Russia dilemma amid talk of Xi-Trump-Putin summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25524e6268ed69a51382738a422c7d99dc68187691c09f2e64b7bc4ae5756af5</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beijing-faces-its-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427--4d68b234d525.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beijing-faces-its-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China is forced to tread carefully as it considers hosting a meeting between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, and Donald Trump. While the optics are sure to favor Moscow, Beijing is risking its image at the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Cyber attacks and hybrid warfare: Germany gives sweeping powers to its police and intelligence services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dff8c122dccba71563e9938270e5b04f4f75cf2e61622822ed0157e65730449</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyber-attacks-and-hybrid-warfare-germany-gives-sweeping-powers-to-its-police-and-intelligence-servic/a-79941507--8b38eb9f8681.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyber-attacks-and-hybrid-warfare-germany-gives-sweeping-powers-to-its-police-and-intelligence-services/a-79941507?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Drone sightings and cyberattacks have heightened security concerns. How are the police preparing to meet these challenges? And how do intelligence services plan to counter threats from both domestic and foreign sources?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's wiretapping scandal opens a political fault line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7948941f51eb91b897abd4d8322d0ab2539bfc0f853d28d8362d9737678cf134</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753--0451bf449bfd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senior police officers are accused of illegally monitoring President Prabowo Subianto, exposing rival networks within Indonesia's security establishment and renewing concerns about political misuse of surveillance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is the AI bubble bursting just as Anthropic goes public?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48a412ed91a48a629e68db30c22960227c24f4a67516e381fd917d2fb4bb14ac</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537--10f78cdc2264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sharp sell-off in tech stocks after the US midterms has cast doubt on Anthropic's looming IPO. Yet with hundreds of billions still being invested, some think the AI party is still in full swing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Nmecha won't repeat controversial goal celebration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f0b199cafda31aac409bfae55ac63e9fa7ff855596e4a3f57b47026cba0efba</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994--cc5ab533247b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany head coach Jürgen Klopp says that midfielder Felix Nmecha will not repeat a goal celebration that sparked controversy over the past week. Germany are set to face Serbia and the Netherlands in the Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parliament agrees on debt-laden 2027 budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47ae9456f9d7e0c56650ceb5ac79026b47dd05de4256e4aa0897458e0978290e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897--be62c4ec3578.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The budget committee in the Bundestag worked into the night to sign off on next year's spending plans. These include levels of new debt only eclipsed once, at the height of the COVID pandemic. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Czechia braces for massive protest against public media reform plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ba3e587347d4c21f960854935901aa3e0feb356d7a43befc8a480620c1a8acb</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-public-media-reform-plans/a-79933533--a08ee7cdb27e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-public-media-reform-plans/a-79933533?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fast-tracked bill to cut public media funding has sparked strikes, rallies and fears for the independence of public broadcasting in Czechia. A massive protest is planned for Prague on Sunday.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Could lack of money sink TFFF rainforest fund before it even launches?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ce451411ab893eab8d6be053b5cd9f033a127f6f03c11977a4db7234bce757c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673--227abf2cebee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TFFF rainforest fund aims to make forest conservation more profitable than deforestation. But a lack of money may prevent it from getting off the ground.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian activist and Nobel Peace Prize winner Narges Mohammadi shares her story in memoir</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ab8e2b40260dffb9f5d4cc58090d68f6a67f6c8a3b16485dd16d0696a1ffb0b</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167--a983bd7e2dcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Written and smuggled out of prison, the 2023 Nobel Prize laureate's memoir reveals the cost of defying Iran's regime and fighting for freedom.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders tussle over whom to send to Ukraine, Russia peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:993c4823a1a1a59b341632e54d497ca82ec19e85abd500e1dcb94f6d22a2b0a6</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468--127d08162dcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A seat at the table for Europe now appears likely following comments by a US envoy who just held talks with Putin. But who will take that seat remains unclear.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can the EU make it harder to trick consumers online?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64c5dd77ee6dc28a715744179bbc010a984eeac8a4f33fdd0e65f1c8388b083b</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T17:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-eu-make-it-harder-to-trick-consumers-online/a-79933447--856c99598d6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-the-eu-make-it-harder-to-trick-consumers-online/a-79933447?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants to curb subscription traps, misleading sales tactics and features that keep people scrolling. What would the proposed Digital Fairness Act change, and does it go far enough?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What have the talks with Russia and the US in Abu Dhabi achieved for Ukraine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c9da44a3f49db00a886a1e6db85a5e8614e16d65996db132d755900ad25413d</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-have-the-talks-with-russia-and-the-us-in-abu-dhabi-achieved-for-ukraine/a-79930613--89b8a9b8f641.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-have-the-talks-with-russia-and-the-us-in-abu-dhabi-achieved-for-ukraine/a-79930613?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The first trilateral talks between Ukraine, the US and Russia in nine months have ended with an agreement on exchanging prisoners. Does this mark a genuine breakthrough and a step toward peace?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary eases abortion restrictions in women's rights overhaul</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15087bea76abc9fe67463f6bc1e6fbc23a24f0906acf6ba80dc4ae538d7484d5</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-eases-abortion-rules/a-79931614--3bb42fe8feff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-eases-abortion-restrictions-in-women-s-rights-overhaul/a-79931614?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The reforms mark a break the the conservative policies of former PM Viktor Orban. The controversial "heartbeat regulation" is to be scrapped and women are to be better protected against violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK court convicts 2 Iranian men of spying on journalists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ad63f926850b0c13df9a75ad37e206b613e21268eef3563a444f0f912eacd20</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583--9da85f420d5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has found two Iranian citizens guilty of surveilling reporters for a Persian-language television station critical of Iran's government. One was also convicted of planning a violent attack against them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: Spy row, affairs leave Nvidia without its rockstar CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abd087e8d5d781a68353847bc88b4e3cdbf97e3a57c1e990376fd88a51efcae8</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972--e6a7da621d57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang, who built Nvidia into the world’s dominant AI chipmaker, is stepping down as CEO over extramarital affairs. DW examines how losing its figurehead will affect the firm and the US-China AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>What are fossil fuels?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8feede44b63e3836545601dce94f72b204969414a9023570f3170c87f04e9939</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540--1920eabf4714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">They are in our shampoo bottles, power our cars and heat our homes. But what actually are fossil fuels, and why do they matter?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police raid chapters of Gremium MC biker gang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48825ddf95394ece3ff115a1f884ac90c2bbe67784ecf2ab7c794aef8fc009d6</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T09:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-raid-chapters-of-gremium-mc-biker-gang/live-79926275--65b7228f3ec1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-raid-chapters-of-gremium-mc-biker-gang/live-79926275?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in southwestern Germany launched major early-morning operations against a biker gang. The state of Baden-Württemberg is outlawing three of its chapters. Meanwhile, unions are planning more strikes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bundeswehr study exposes widespread sexual harassment in German military</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:841cc751d787b2b9084b5c20b359924ad84caf0a9502e3e3c7448123b41356ef</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundeswehr-study-exposes-widespread-sexual-harassment-in-german-military/a-79926359--0cec81791758.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundeswehr-study-exposes-widespread-sexual-harassment-in-german-military/a-79926359?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sexual misconduct in the Bundeswehr is far more widespread than previously known, with younger women disproportionately affected. Defense Minister Boris Pistorius has called for a policy of "zero tolerance."</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Intelligent women get less help at work, study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0247ab6596a4299f7a2290f89f1588dd5507abd31df17d27d28ae87ad7e8d326</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881--d3f9551f1647.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women who scored high on intelligence tests were seen as more hostile by their teammates and got less help, a new study finds. High-scoring men faced no such penalty. Research explains why.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Fears of rising antisemitism in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b14c5f375330736f6b4789a8696fedb7c1290d71f88ba5e26aefb7818ee9b0ec</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T20:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fears-of-rising-antisemitism-in-europe/a-79921783--20638e7d2425.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fears-of-rising-antisemitism-in-europe/a-79921783?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Holocaust survivor Regina Sluszny commemorates the victims of Auschwitz as Jewish communities across Europe face growing hostility. What does the promise of "Never Again" mean for Jewish life in Europe today?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Why the integration of immigrants in Germany remains a challenge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a85540c771f6d92a7c09c3509c0eff32a18464fa888972baa7f6b1380d761c8</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T17:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-integration-of-immigrants-in-germany-remains-a-challenge/a-79923241--a319297bc2a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-integration-of-immigrants-in-germany-remains-a-challenge/a-79923241?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Federal Office for Migration and Refugees has released a new Integration Report. It found that while the integration of people with a migrant background is improving, violent youth remain a problem.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Democracy study: One-quarter of Germans want a right-wing authoritarian dictatorship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e4063feaa37b95f2344431b1fb4510afe18964b91f3a660da7723ee0e18bced</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/democracy-study-one-quarter-of-germans-want-a-right-wing-authoritarian-dictatorship/a-79922718--e6377f13d887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/democracy-study-one-quarter-of-germans-want-a-right-wing-authoritarian-dictatorship/a-79922718?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD's electoral successes point to a new trend in Germany: Prejudice, resentment, and extremism are on the rise. A new study suggests satisfaction with democracy is at a low ebb.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29ede6cd734494378a8f4c971c9f497ea709237fa3b817bd1992d64a4a31a4e0</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73d0619a382e74160b32972aa754da9864d6588d4bfd94febd76083d64af9303</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>DW Science explainer on the default mode network: what your brain does when you aren't focusing on anything, and why it's important.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cd8bc2d8fdb89df65f8cf6bdf90cadfda7c218a7b38436fb33bb4d9c5c60c6e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-an/a-79908787--cf91bcf53b1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-anything-and-why-it-s-important/a-79908787?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doing nothing might be the ultimate brain hack. When you're bored, the brain goes into default mode network. It's not only healthy for you, but it may also shape the very essence of your identity.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany slips in climate protection rankings as other countries make gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3aba3bb788085b93e71965ea0533d98eba0ac5e42140035a4904bfd9aaca3d2a</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635--edb7d622928e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record renewable energy growth is driving climate progress in some countries, but Germany and many major emitters are falling behind.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>British counterterrorism police arrest US soldier accused of spying on behalf of Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e49f5bbe7d79dcb569520ded634a041c0d3a71b660e9c0834d1057844316bee</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240--5991e0a904a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A member of the US Army has been arrested near Gloucester in England. Police said he was suspected of espionage activity in connection with Russia. Investigators from the US and UK are involved in the probe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK Privy Council overrules Trinidad and Tobago gay sex law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10f240614f2f911e59245f83bd8a86ac1d4b692ff7b5a1dcb50bb3161bac1fda</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163--f186aba38925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has overturned a Trinidad and Tobago law criminalizing consensual sexual relations between male same-sex couples. As a result of the colonial legacy, it is the independent country's last court of appeal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Victims of Nazi war in Poland call on Germany for support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b1e897a4f099f4641fa7dfba41d3dfaf41c6a52b7a39cd66075efe1a45e5da4</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311--36756d6320e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 80 years after the end of World War II, Polish victims of the Nazi regime are still waiting for a "humanitarian gesture" from Germany. The 2027 draft budget hasn't left them much hope for possible reparations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran denies role in fridge hack, France summons ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86155543decb5df7bd763d31769a1f93154b7943b5ed4818f32a66dcfacecd56</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206--6d0355211a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France has said it rules "nothing" out in response to a cyberattack on supermarket refrigeration units. Iran, however, said it categorically rejected Paris' "baseless and one-sided accusations" of IRGC involvement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5928c786253c35dfacbdafb9ba0fd02bf1288b2b586408f4b16d8b831eb8bc61</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edc2d50430b91ea26bde9293bfd6273866f84b54fae3a1276eaee49c3c756a56</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Megaspeed and the battle to go high-end Nvidia chips into China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8653c746808904868fed3882a9f8a5c2a78398ac19451a9650f120656140eb5f</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129--5e400fbb45fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy has shone a light on Megaspeed, the company she worked for. It is under investigation in the US for smuggling Nvidia chips into China, which it denies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria highway pileup kills 12, dozens injured: PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83698520e146387a4147e4732784548268f1271cd2f2195bb16a3ad7421b3645</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-highway-pileup-kills-12-dozens-injured-pm/a-79907978--e4c51329b4c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-highway-pileup-kills-12-dozens-injured-pm/a-79907978?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 12 people were killed and dozens injured in a series of crashes caused by thick fog in Bulgaria. Police, firefighters and paramedics were dispatched to the scene for the rescue operation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund's Felix Nmecha and the question of religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f36120b23d51b59c691959a355ce2fb95d9d7fcaab26725215f7da06aeffad83</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432--cd7bb6e11389.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Felix Nmecha's "Crowns down" celebration has drawn criticism from a Borussia Dortmund fan club, reopening debate over faith, inclusion and religious messaging in football.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Online disinformation rife after Krakow mass shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32898ceef6cedef953432677f7cb5f64978737d4c32ad7f24d66d56c981d45b2</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-online-disinformation-rife-after-krakow-mass-shooting/a-79900620--80ad1afffb68.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-online-disinformation-rife-after-krakow-mass-shooting/a-79900620?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fake and AI-manipulated images spread online in the hours after the Krakow attack, fueling false narratives about the mass shooting. DW Fact Check examined what's real, and what isn't.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why electrification is the climate game changer we need</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cede6bf2b4894e6745a515b8505919b8b5d3031b2cc25334785cbadff5623d6</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-electrification-is-the-climate-game-changer-we-need/a-79615979--0dbca6445640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-electrification-is-the-climate-game-changer-we-need/a-79615979?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From EVs and electric buses on the road, heat pumps warming homes and solar panels powering appliances, the shift to electrifying tech is already in full swing. But what exactly does "electrification" mean?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Will Australia push for fossil fuel exit at UN talks?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd8e67dd000aa4476b1751f009c2154feec11020adaecfa373fde55e2b38cf3c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-australia-push-for-fossil-fuel-exit-at-un-talks/a-79782066--e866c53d355a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-australia-push-for-fossil-fuel-exit-at-un-talks/a-79782066?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The heat is on Australia as chief negotiator at the COP31 UN climate conference to forge a path away from coal and gas, and to protect Pacific neighbors facing rising sea levels.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>US, Russia, Ukraine wrap up talks with prisoner exchange agreement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f4d621bda98ffe396c8548cf3acda872cfa83b450906829710efc41c334b067</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T07:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-russia-ukraine-wrap-up-talks-with-prisoner-exchange-agreement/live-79906232--00cfe2e7daba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-russia-ukraine-wrap-up-talks-with-prisoner-exchange-agreement/live-79906232?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Peace talks between Russia, Ukraine and the US concluded in the United Arab Emirates. The two day talks were the first such meeting since February. DW has the latest updates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why malnutrition can go unnoticed, and what that means for our health</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:289e347ffd05bf0f96cc5338cc60aedbb18fccf5894845eb2f35769ebea8a417</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-malnutrition-can-go-unnoticed-and-what-that-means-for-our-health/a-79871016--a7247c0af1e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-malnutrition-can-go-unnoticed-and-what-that-means-for-our-health/a-79871016?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 2 billion people worldwide suffer from nutrient deficiencies, most of them in the Global South. The health consequences can be devastating.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war oil shock drives dip in global emissions, study shows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:595ce7e3f11005c14da7419966a94e51722805c317a717d128306f9b2d7947eb</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T03:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937--fec20d5dba18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Global carbon emissions are expected to fall slightly in 2026, but not because of major progress on climate action. Instead, it's high energy prices following the US attack on Iran that's driving the trend.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>New trilateral talks on Ukraine war in Abu Dhabi: What to expect?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2b58bee2963ed9de67b31a5fc2cd1a35a15ad287367e598c270f5c918a048c3</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T23:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-trilateral-talks-on-ukraine-war-in-abu-dhabi-what-to-expect/a-79905734--3c6da76b72e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-trilateral-talks-on-ukraine-war-in-abu-dhabi-what-to-expect/a-79905734?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian and Russian representatives last met in February for talks on ending the war, but the same sticking points remain. Ukraine continues to demand security guarantees, which is a non-starter for Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia: Independent Novaya Gazeta shuts its Moscow newsroom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a81d5d08c63e38209233d5ad30a4179b381b1d584934d78afc17815e1df826b6</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-independent-novaya-gazeta-shuts-its-moscow-newsroom/a-79899827--d187f3fbc3fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-independent-novaya-gazeta-shuts-its-moscow-newsroom/a-79899827?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The investigative newspaper is closing its doors after Russian authorities labeled it a "foreign agent" and ordered it vacate its Moscow premises.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's ice hockey team says Russia replacing it at World Juniors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a039c2928504087300fe2c2066c1425ba1deed72c91fb893bbfab81bfc988232</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844--43300d3ba1be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The wrangling over Russia's return to international ice hockey continues, with Norway saying it has been kicked out of the next major tournament to accommodate Russia. Switzerland has joined a "boycott."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>37 years after fall of Berlin Wall: How divided are Germans?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9434f4307d8eb2af8f868acd63caceb3ca8f2ae52561154db7aff03288b7f0fc</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/37-years-after-fall-of-berlin-wall-how-divided-are-germans/a-79877461--471b79fce1fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/37-years-after-fall-of-berlin-wall-how-divided-are-germans/a-79877461?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three artists share their thoughts on the reunification of East and West Germany. How do they perceive a shared "we" and what gives them cause for optimism?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: CDU names Ilse Aigner as candidate for president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06d5adad004effa93fb563e78dbc4d409531d84e48a42713c0135134326339d8</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T12:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-names-ilse-aigner-as-candidate-for-president/a-79898143--f4c7d81c5dcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-names-ilse-aigner-as-candidate-for-president/a-79898143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The steering committtee of the CDU have announced Bavarian politician Ilse Aigner as presidential candidate. This gives her a good chance of becoming the first woman to occupy the role.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU aims to pick new ECB chief by year-end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b1f5be558928df0976fc053da2fd08b9c7bf32b877d1d889eeec293ded608c2</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-aims-to-pick-new-ecb-chief-by-year-end/a-79898169--04bae0a2e38e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-aims-to-pick-new-ecb-chief-by-year-end/a-79898169?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Christine Lagarde's decision to step down early as head of the European Central Bank (ECB) has put the European Union on a tight schedule. The bloc expects to pick a new ECB chief by the end of December.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why Nvidia CEO's affair with alleged Chinese spy matters for AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a3c542873ed49846d92e0387fff76dc7400886487e038719bcf53ff547a3a0c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-nvidia-ceo-s-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy-matters-for-ai-race/a-79898338--07d9155781b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-nvidia-ceo-s-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy-matters-for-ai-race/a-79898338?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has apologized for an affair with a woman the US believes was spying for China. The story could have profound implications for the world's most valuable company and the global AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Who is Ilse Aigner, leading candidate for Germany's next president?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c71edb6c764ff8257c3579c1cdf31d6beba6fc44a95bab314f59bd011655e6fa</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-is-ilse-aigner-leading-candidate-for-germany-s-next-president/a-79898848--5540ac90be2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-is-ilse-aigner-leading-candidate-for-germany-s-next-president/a-79898848?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She would be the first female president and the first Christian Social Union politician to hold Germany's highest office. Ilse Aigner is the favored candidate for the Federal Convention vote on January 30.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Germany marks fateful date of November 9</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e47a08799cc2518f1288a31d228f80ec970033a8661f4c3ac88e73f4c9f3cc93</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-marks-fateful-date-of-november-9/live-79895613--b598062ac50d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-marks-fateful-date-of-november-9/live-79895613?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany is commemorating the Nazi-led November pogroms 88 years ago. Events are also being held to mark the anniversary of the fall of the Berlin Wall in 1989. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Krakow mass shooting suspect has died in hospital, police in Poland say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c2653ff6627c3c41f998e86a2274d48af72911b9b56c357ca388d9354456920</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T06:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/krakow-mass-shooting-suspect-has-died-in-hospital-police-in-poland-say/a-79895626--6dfb07803fa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/krakow-mass-shooting-suspect-has-died-in-hospital-police-in-poland-say/a-79895626?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The alleged gunman who killed six people in a shooting spree in the Polish city of Krakow has died of injuries sustained in a shootout with police, authorities say.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Chancellor Merz to nominate Aigner for president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72e2c642e62689cb0ee1ef94208bb14ae99e383f06296d65f88b89c77472ed7b</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T19:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-chancellor-merz-to-nominate-aigner-for-president/live-79883533--d347f58eed72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-chancellor-merz-to-nominate-aigner-for-president/live-79883533?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz announced that he will nominate Ilse Aigner for federal president, paving the way for her to be the first woman to hold the office. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Never Again!': Holocaust remembrance under pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228e90170c23f60779f2445b6a1399bc7f29ae6c46f4306b0cdc430f9981d18a</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/never-again-holocaust-remembrance-under-pressure/a-79840894--861f4756e8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/never-again-holocaust-remembrance-under-pressure/a-79840894?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Only a few Holocaust survivors remain who can share their stories firsthand. Meanwhile, voices calling for an end to what they describe as a "cult of guilt" are growing louder. How can Holocaust remembrance survive?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>As COP31 Antalya kicks off, can world move beyond big promises?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b6d0bb11541b8aa9ac8cf81fce00036a2f92898714343feb1c8d208aa0c6b4d</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T05:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366--3ff0bee69cef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Droughts, floods and extreme heat are upping the pressure on delegates at the UN climate talks in Antalya, Turkey. Can countries move beyond pledges to concrete action?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Armenia's selective prosecution: A threat to EU relations?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:900a10a4ca388e2fd066f9848c6f7b4a212a14430f38a6973b0f6d0254af6beb</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/armenia-s-selective-prosecution-a-threat-to-eu-relations/a-79878159--345ae9a3ae32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/armenia-s-selective-prosecution-a-threat-to-eu-relations/a-79878159?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Brussels has refrained from harsh criticism, Armenian civil society has warned of selective justice against opposition figures. Could the EU's pragmatic stance risk repeating past mistakes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><en